ALBUKHR Testnet Investor Financial Integrity Hardening v1
Applied status
This hardening was applied to the ALBUKHR Testnet Supabase project on 2026-11-07. The current SQL structure was verified after application. The SQL test used in CI is deliberately isolated to temporary tables and is not run against the live Supabase database.
Do not re-run the original DDL patch against the already-patched Testnet database. The constraint names already exist there. The original DDL/audit bundle is retained in ALBUKHR_TESTNET_FINANCIAL_INTEGRITY_HARDENING_v1.zip from the conversation.
Database invariants now enforced
stakes.user_id + pi_uid + network must reference one matching users row.
stakes.project_id + project_code + network must reference one matching projects row.
withdrawal_requests.stake_id is NOT NULL.
A withdrawal's user_id + pi_uid + network must reference one matching user.
A withdrawal's project_id + project_code + network must reference one matching project.
A withdrawal's stake_id + pi_uid + project_id + project_code + network must reference the exact parent stake.
complete_testnet_withdrawal_and_ledger() performs explicit owner/project/network checks and uses an empty search_path.
Added child-side indexes
stakes_user_identity_idx
stakes_project_network_idx
withdrawal_requests_user_identity_idx
withdrawal_requests_project_network_idx
withdrawal_requests_stake_owner_project_idx
The post-change Supabase Performance Advisor no longer reported these five new foreign keys as unindexed.
Operational controls
The settlement function remains SECURITY DEFINER and server-only: anon and authenticated cannot execute it; service_role can.
Testnet treasury remains active while staking_policy_active remains false.
Staking, withdrawals and Pi payments remain locked.
No stake, withdrawal, payment or ledger transaction rows were created or edited by the hardening.
Test boundaries
The new GitHub Actions workflow runs:
Financial Core smoke tests.
Financial UI smoke tests.
Static checks that the hardening and post-apply verification contract files contain the expected safeguards.
A PostgreSQL 16 service test using temporary tables. It accepts a matching withdrawal relationship and rejects owner, project and Mainnet/Testnet mismatches, then rolls back.
This CI suite does not connect to Supabase and does not claim to execute a real Pi payment or a production settlement. Those remain separate, controlled tests and must not be used to enable live transaction controls.
